# Allowlist, not a blocklist. The working directory also holds ~5 GB of
# reverse-engineering byproducts (memory dumps, pointer-scan results, watch logs)
# and the one-off RE scripts that produced them. Those are how the memory offsets
# were FOUND, not part of the app — the findings themselves live in FINDINGS.md
# and config/dd2.offsets.json, which is what actually matters.
#
# So: ignore everything, then re-include the app.
# (Note: gitignore has no trailing comments — a '#' after a path is part of the
# pattern, not a comment. Keep every comment on its own line.)

/*
!.gitignore
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!README.md
!FINDINGS.md
!src/
!config/

# --- src/main: the app. The RE tooling sitting next to it stays untracked:
# scanner.js, globalHunt.js, pointerScan.js, testChains.js, findOrigin.js,
# findCellIndex.js, verifyCellIndex.js, watch.js, globalWatch.js, ctLogger.js,
# ctSnapshot.js, readCtAddresses.js, readStatic.js, compareStatic.js,
# analyzeRebase.js, probeMapLib.js, smokeTest.js
src/main/*
!src/main/index.js
!src/main/memoryReader.js
!src/main/win32Input.js
!src/main/overlayWindow.js
!src/main/overlayConfig.js
!src/main/configStore.js

# --- src/renderer: all of it is the app, nothing to exclude.

# --- config: the hard-won findings and the calibration.
# config/overlay.json and config/view.json are per-machine runtime state the app
# rewrites as you drag sliders and zoom; the code carries working defaults
# (overlayConfig.js), so a fresh clone runs without them.
config/*
!config/dd2.offsets.json
!config/calibration.json
